DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

Determine whether the Boolean expressions are equivalent:
[`(((((C \land C)) \land ((D \oplus D)))) \land C), (((C \land C)) \lor ((((D \oplus D)) \land C)))`]
Enter 1 if equivalent and 0 otherwise.
[_____]{answer=>0,width=>1}
---

Determine whether the Boolean expressions are equivalent:
[`(B \oplus C), (((B \lor C)) \lor (\neg ((B \land C))))`]
Enter 1 if equivalent and 0 otherwise.
[_____]{0}
---

Determine whether the Boolean expressions are equivalent:
[`(E \to D), ((\neg E) \lor D)`]
Enter 1 if equivalent and 0 otherwise.
[_____]{answer=>1,width=>1}
---

Evaluate the Boolean expression:
[`(((B \leftrightarrow B)) \oplus ((E \oplus E)))`]
When:
- E = \mathsf{F}
- B = \mathsf{T}
- C = \mathsf{T}
Enter 1 for True and 0 for False.
[_____]{answer=>1,width=>1}
---

Determine whether the Boolean expressions are equivalent:
[`(C \to ((C \to C))), ((\neg C) \lor ((C \to C)))`]
Enter 1 if equivalent and 0 otherwise.
[_____]{answer=>1,width=>1}
---

Determine whether the Boolean expressions are equivalent:
[`((\neg E) \to ((B \leftrightarrow A))), (((B \leftrightarrow A)) \to (\neg E))`]
Enter 1 if equivalent and 0 otherwise.
[_____]{answer=>0,width=>1}
---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
